{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"746843387432534156","content":"**Oath of Arachne**\nThe Oath of Arachne is a curious and often unheard-of order of paladins, who model their virtues after those of the humble spider. To those familiar with the order, they are known as spider-knights, snare-soldiers, or ironclad crawlers. Binding oneself to the Oath of Arachne is often a difficult task, as few established orders exist, and tend to be more localized than many others. The Oath of Arachne is also home to all kinds, including those with not-so-pure intentions. Undertakers of this oath are often followers of Lolth, Anansi, or another local spider-related deity, such as the New Orleans demigod Web. \n\n**Tennants of Arachne**\nThe tenants of the Oath of Arachne tend to vary from order to order, especially between orders following different deities. But regardless of how they are changed, the tenants tend to follow this basic form.\n`Know Your Enemy`\nIn order to best solve a problem, you must first understand that problem. The easiest solution is often not the best.\n`Kill With Purpose`\nJust as spiders kill to feed themselves or their young, a foe should not be killed for no reason. An enemy's body should be honored and made use of. \n`Be Patient, be Prepared`\nDo not blindly seek out your enemy, lest you end up making more in their place. By your words and deeds you will make yourself known and enemies will seek you out. Be ready, just as a spider spins its web.\n`Continue the Cycle`\nJust as life and death pass fluidly into one another, so should your tenets pass on to the next generation. Your actions must create lasting change, not just a momentary reprieve.","created_at":"2020-08-23T04:20:00.743000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-23T04:20:16.641000Z","id":"746946825260498946","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
